# ─── Personal data — NEVER commit ────────────────────────────────────────
# rsvp_data.db is written next to the app on every run and holds real
# colleagues' names, email addresses and gift-contribution amounts. It was
# committed to this public repository once already; scripts/check_no_pii.py
# now fails CI if it comes back.
rsvp_data.db
*.db
*.db-journal
*.db-wal
*.db-shm

# Exported reports and rosters contain the same personal data. Every
# spreadsheet this app reads or writes is one of them - Participant_List_*,
# *_Report, RSVP_History_export, the recipient template - so all of them are
# ignored, not a list of names. A list of names missed four of the files the
# app actually writes (Codex review of PR #1). A spreadsheet that genuinely
# belongs in git is added with `git add -f` and still has to pass
# .pii-allowlist.
*.xlsx
*.xlsm
*.xls

# Local user overrides written by history.py
fixed_wording_overrides.json
prompt_overrides.json

# ─── Python ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*.egg-info/
.venv/
venv/
.pytest_cache/
.ruff_cache/

# ─── OS / editor ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
Thumbs.db
desktop.ini
.DS_Store
.vscode/
.idea/

